    "summary": "Soaring Crazy Fingers, fiery Standing On The Moon, jazzy Dark Star",
    "blurb": "Highlights include a blistering Crazy Fingers, a soaring Standing On The Moon solo and an expansive Dark Star. Vince’s keyboards add texture throughout, while the drummers drive the high‑energy peaks.",
    "review": "December 12, 1992 at the Oakland Coliseum delivers a vibrant late‑career set that feels both contemplative and explosive. The first set opens with a tight Jack Straw into a lackluster Bertha, but quickly lifts with Bird Song’s lyrical grace. The second set is where the magic truly unfolds – Crazy Fingers erupts with Jerry’s trademark “crazy” licks, segueing into a soaring Standing On The Moon solo that many reviewers call “fiery.” Dark Star rolls out as a jazzy, space‑filled journey, buoyed by Vince Welnick’s assertive keyboards and the twin‑drum thunder of Mickey and Bill. The night caps off with a rapturous Rain encore that leaves listeners on an emotional high.\n\nAcross the best soundboard capture (Stonebear), the mix is crystal‑clear, letting every nuance shine – from Jerry’s soaring leads to Vince’s vocal harmonies and the crisp percussion work. While a few reviewers note a slow first set and a brief lyrical stumble in Bertha, the overall performance is consistently praised as “on fire,” with multiple recordings highlighting the same high points, confirming this show as a standout late‑1990s gem.",
